     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The Multiplication Rule of Counting says that if there are <i>n</i> ways to accomplish one task and <i>m</i> ways to accomplish a second task, then there are <span data-math=\"n{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}m\"></span> ways to accomplish both tasks. You can tack on additional tasks by multiplying the number of ways to accomplish those tasks to your previous product.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"18{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}30{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}540\"></span></p>\n"
    },
    {
